Hi geomorph community,

I have a concern wether my correction for a random effect nested within another random effect is correct (tree/leaf). I have fitted the following models and when compared indicate that the unique allometries model is appropriated.

fit3.common <- lm.rrpp(logSize ~ faltitude + tree/leaf, SS.type = "I",
data = dombeyi.gdf, iter = 999, print.progress = FALSE)

fit3.unique <- lm.rrpp(logSize ~ faltitude * tree/leaf, SS.type = "I",
                       data = dombeyi.gdf, iter = 9999, print.progress = FALSE)

anova(fit3.common,fit3.unique)

#                                                       ResDf Df   RSS     SS             MS     Rsq        F          Z    P Pr(>F)
# logSize ~ faltitude + tree/leaf (Null)   636  1 3.4203                 0.32080
# logSize ~ faltitude * tree/leaf             594 42 1.9527 1.4676 0.034942 0.61223 10.629 12.302 1e-04

Is the mean-square (MS) error estimation correct?

anova(fit3.unique, effect.type = "F",
      error = c("Residuals","faltitude:tree:leaf","faltitude:tree:leaf", "Residuals"))

                   Df               SS           MS          Rsq              F               Z       Pr(>F)
